From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] incremental render, overlap fix, and rendering fixes

Implements incremental rendering via an accumulation surface that
persists across frames, so only newly-typed characters are drawn per
frame instead of re-rendering all ~32K chars from scratch.  Pre-computes
color doubles at init time.

Fixes:
- Double y-increment on line wrap (was incremented twice).
- Antialiased glyph edge blending with stale scrolled content (clears
  each character-run cell with CAIRO_OPERATOR_SOURCE before
  cairo_show_text).
- Null-termination of render buffer before cairo_show_text (UB).
- Rest-of-line background cleared after each text run so shorter
  lines on a given row don't inherit stale characters from a
  previous scroll cycle.
- xjack_add_char array compaction resetting accum_char_count/first_paint
  so incremental rendering resumes after off-screen chars are pruned.

---
 render/effect_xjack.c | 262 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 render/effect_xjack.h |  14 +++
 2 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

diff --git a/render/effect_xjack.c b/render/effect_xjack.c
